==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|receptāculum||reservoir, receptacle|lang=la}}, from {{term|receptō||I receive back or again, recover|lang=la}}, frequentative of {{term|recipiō||I receive; hold back, reserve|lang=la}}, from {{term|re-||back, again|lang=la}} + {{term|capiō||I hold|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[container]].
# {{context|botany|lang=en}} The part of the [[flower]] [[stalk]] ([[peduncle]] or [[pedicel]]) to which the floral parts are attached; also [[torus]].
## In the ''[[Asteraceae]]'', the end of the peduncle to which all of the florets of the flower head are attached.
# {{context|electricity|US|lang=en}} A contact device installed at an [[outlet]] for the connection of an attachment plug and flexible cord to supply portable equipment or appliances.

